WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:12.580 align:start position:0%
 
do  fallout 4 is a dense and engrossing RPG  set in a post nuclear apocalypse version  of Boston once known for its historical  significance and modern academic  prestige Boston is now defined by ruined  buildings and vile mutants death and  desperation surround you yet you can't  look away it's hard to resist the allure  of unravelling mysteries and discovering  forgotten sanctuaries as you dig deeper  into myriad enclaves that called a  wasteland home go where you wish deal  with people in problems however you want  but be sure to watch your back it's not  unusual to find yourself hunted by  oafish mutants while you struggle with  wounded limbs radiation poisoning or an  unfortunate lack of ammo you could take  shelter in a dilapidated train station  but it's not worth the risk  scavengers may be lying in wait instead  you inject yourself with drugs lots of  them to get back on your feet with your  heightened perception and strength  giving you the edge you need to cut down  your pursuers with your final precious  bullets the heavy dusts of stimulus will  leave you addled but at least you can  survive to fight in search for traces of  your family another day it's wonderfully  tense moments like this that make  fallout for such an engaging and  intoxicating experience when fallout 4  shows its wrinkles it feels like a  direct extension of fallout 3 rather  than a sequel years in the making in so  many ways it shows a lack of progress  however the more time you spend with the  game the less you care when you're  enraptured with characters struggling  with difficult decisions and engaged in  combat you no longer care that something  could look better or be more organized  you may examine the game closely and  recognize flaws but when you put the  controller down you think about the  friend you betrayed the shifting tide of  an incredible battle or the moment you  opened a drawer and found someone's  discarded effects making you wonder how  they felt before the bombs fell  combat is comprised of melee attacks and  gunplay with a massive number of weapon  variations to experiment with you can  hit a bloody homerun with an enemy's  head in a spiked bat or wield a sniper  rifle and pick off jerks from afar both  methods work opening up a vast range of  combat scenarios to explore in the  middle you can even modify your weapons  and other equipment by salvaging  everyday objects scattered throughout  Boston allowing you to tweak your  arsenal and extend its usefulness in  significant ways at any moment you have  the option to switch between third or  first-person perspective on the fly but  more importantly you can choose to fight  in real time or within an RPG rooted  command system you grow very familiar  with vats the system you can use to plot  every pull of the trigger it's an  extension of the same mechanic from  fallout 3 and Fallout New Vegas but  activating vats in those games pause the  action completely now it merely slows  down time and you're vulnerable when  picking your target as a result the  advantage to using vats versus fighting  in real time is that it gives you the  ability to aim for specific body parts  and consider how likely you are to hit  your mark and how much damage you will  inflict if you do the mix of utility and  strategy that it presents is encouraging  and it's a far more enjoyable and  effective tool than real time shooting  which is functional but lacking the  finesse found and dedicated shooting  games  FASS also frames your actions with  cinematic flair on occasion showcasing  the brutality of combat was tiring  while Boston steams beyond salvation you  can influence the lives of some locals  by constructing sanctuaries for them to  live in scrap junk that you find  throughout the city and you can erect  shelters establish small vegetable  gardens and fortify defense systems  there is a lot you can build and the  process is easy but unless you love to  be creative you may not find this  pursuit all that interesting beyond a  few side quests the game hardly  motivates you to partake in construction  there's something to be said for the  contrast between killing monsters and  providing aid to those in need but the  rewards really extend beyond gratitude  and some experience points with the  dense city to explore and greater  rewards to reap it's all too easy to  ignore this feature altogether from  farmland to financial districts and  throughout the depths of dangerous  ghettos like opportunities to profit  explore and form relationships though  you can choose to befriend betray or  belittle people you interact with the  two-word summations don't always do a  good job of forecasting the extent of  your eventual dialogue I was often  surprised by my character's tone and  choice of words fallout 4 is an  involving RPG with a wealth of stories  to explore and activities to engage in  but it's also an old-looking game you  immediately noticed poor character  models muddy textures and a bevy of  glitches poor organization and  accessibility makes managing your  inventory and navigating the world map  feel arduous the companions that you can  bring into battle are more trouble than  they're worth they often lose their way  and are difficult to control and you  need them to perform a certain task  in fact you feel lucky when they appear  next to you in battle because you grow  so accustomed to them getting stuck in a  stairwell or between two rocks with  Boston at your mercy you'll ultimately  have the power to push it over the edge  or rescue it from ruin but this isn't a  matter of good versus evil  you need to make difficult decisions  that force you to question your morals  and what it means to be human after the  final act of the main story you're left  to continue your adventure and though  some quests seem trite in the face of  the story's main conclusion they still  take you to fascinating places and  reward your curiosity fallout 4 is a  strong argument for substance over style  and it's a remarkable open-world RPG  you

